WEBVTT

NOTE English visual guide. Editorial descriptions of on-screen concepts; no spoken narration.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Attention creates a new representation for a position by mixing information from other positions.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
A context-sensitive pronoun motivates the operation. This introductory illustration allows

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
bidirectional context.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.600
The worked example uses four token positions and small vectors so the calculation can be followed by

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.200
hand.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.800
Learned linear projections produce queries, keys and values from the input representations.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.800
A query is compared with each key using a dot product. These comparisons form a row of attention

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.600
scores.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.400
Matrix multiplication QKᵀ computes scores for every query against every key.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.800
Divide the scores by the square root of the key dimension to moderate their scale before softmax.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.400
Apply softmax separately to each score row. The resulting weights are nonnegative and sum to one.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.000
A larger score receives a larger weight relative to the other entries in that row.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.400
Multiply each value vector by its weight and add the results to produce one output vector.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.400
Repeating the operation for every query produces the output matrix: softmax(QKᵀ/√dₖ)V.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.200
The output depends on both the learned projections and the current context. It is not simply a

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.400
lookup of one word.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.200
Causal masking will prevent a position from using future tokens when the task is next-token

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.400
prediction.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Pause and trace a single query: compare keys, scale scores, normalize weights and mix values.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.800
Recap the computation. The next animation adds masks, heads and position information.
